invariant: INV-16
file: src/aead_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: each pass of the open absorbs the bytes at pt in place of the bytes
  at ct. An open in place reads the same bytes, so only a separate output
  shows it: there the pass absorbs bytes it has not written, the tag does
  not match, and the open of a correct record fails.
  bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test opens into a separate output; the script runs
  it for x86-64 under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
pass_hashing(input, pass_counter(index), ct + offset, pt + offset, ct + offset, h, &of_r);
--- new
pass_hashing(input, pass_counter(index), ct + offset, pt + offset, pt + offset, h, &of_r);
